('bmlt-electrolyteabg1-mcq-019','BMLT','BMLT NHPC Licensing','mcq','free',19,'{"question":"A blood gas sample should generally be collected anaerobically to avoid:","translation":"","options":["Gas exchange with air altering results","Clotting of every sample","All electrolyte changes","Hemoglobin degradation immediately"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Air exposure can change PaO2 and PaCO2 and affect pH.","explanationNe":"हावासँग सम्पर्क हुँदा PaO2, PaCO2 र pH बदलिन सक्छ।","topic":"Electrolytes, Blood Gas & Acid–Base Balance"}'::jsonb,true),
